BOTH LEGS, ON A TRIMMED NODE. The partner of pin-cfg-@RELAY@: identical channel
allowlist, so the node keeps exactly one outgoing channel, plus
max_cached_paths = 1 so the return draw collapses too.

Run it ONLY alongside its pin-cfg partner, as their own study. Read the pair:

  pin-cfg-@RELAY@          forward pinned by topology, return free
  pin-cfg-pinned-@RELAY@   forward AND return pinned

The gap between them is what the return leg costs. Neither belongs in a run with
'auto', because the trimmed channel set is node-global -- on a one-channel node
'auto' is not auto, it is this arm without the allowlist to hold it there.

Both carry the allowlist for a reason: without it, the strategy would reopen the
channels you closed during that arm's sessions, un-trimming the node midway
through the study with nothing in the data marking where.
